# Dev Notes 09 — runtime-lifecycle-modularization-v1 first clean module

## Branch

`runtime-lifecycle-modularization-v1`

## Status

First clean modularization slice staged and sandbox verified.

This branch intentionally stops after one low-risk module extraction. Broader lifecycle modularization is deferred until a higher-fidelity modularization plan is available and reviewed.

## Source base

Started from the formatted active-source ZIP:

```text
active-source-truth_runtime-dev-repo-main.zip
```

The source base already included:

```text
docs/dev-notes.07
tests/smokeTestWorkerOperationSerialization.mjs
docs/dev-notes.08
tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
```

So this branch starts after worker operation serialization and the init-reset-without-prior-prompt follow-up test work.

## Purpose

Begin lifecycle modularization conservatively by extracting only pure native-operation policy helpers from `inference.mjs`.

The goal is to improve separation of concerns without changing behavior.

## Implementation summary

Added:

```text
nativeOperationPolicy.mjs
```

The new module owns pure native operation hard-stop policy helpers:

```js
export const VALID_NATIVE_OPERATION_HARD_STOP_KEYS = new Set([
    "enabled",
    "resetModelTimeoutMs",
    "shutdownTimeoutMs",
    "resetSessionTimeoutMs",
    "timeoutAction"
]);

export const VALID_NATIVE_OPERATION_TIMEOUT_ACTIONS = new Set([
    "mark-unhealthy"
]);

export function resolveNativeOperationHardStopConfig(configSnapshot) { ... }

export function createNativeOperationTimeoutError({ operation, sessionId = null, timeoutMs }) { ... }
```

`inference.mjs` now imports:

```js
import {
    createNativeOperationTimeoutError,
    resolveNativeOperationHardStopConfig
} from "./nativeOperationPolicy.mjs";
```

and passes the current config snapshot explicitly:

```js
resolveNativeOperationHardStopConfig(config);
```

## What intentionally stayed in `inference.mjs`

The following behavior-bearing state and coordination helpers remain in `inference.mjs`:

```text
runtimeUnhealthy
createRuntimeUnhealthyError()
assertRuntimeHealthy()
markRuntimeUnhealthy()
waitForNativeOperationBoundary()
```

Reason:

- they close over parent runtime state;
- they are coupled to reset/session/shutdown waiter behavior;
- moving them safely should be a later deliberate lifecycle-state extraction, not part of this first slice.

## Test fixture propagation

Several smoke tests create temporary mock runtime trees using fixed `RUNTIME_FILES` lists. Because `inference.mjs` now imports `nativeOperationPolicy.mjs`, those fixture lists were updated to include the new module.

Updated fixture lists in:

```text
tests/smokeTestContextCreationCancelBoundary.mjs
tests/smokeTestContextCreationRetry.mjs
tests/smokeTestDrainShutdown.mjs
tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
tests/smokeTestNativeOperationHardStopPolicy.mjs
tests/smokeTestWorkerNativeCancellationBoundary.mjs
tests/smokeTestWorkerOperationSerialization.mjs
```

No test assertions or intended behavior were changed.

